/T (passengers, 28 flights, 50 bookings and so on\). The queries demonstrate filtering with WHERE, sorting with ORDER BY, grouping with GROUP BY, filtering groups with HAVING, and the aggregate functions COUNT\(\), SUM\(\), AVG\(\), MIN\(\) and MAX\(\). Each query is followed by its output and a short explanation. Section 7 adds INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE statements. All commands are also in the script basic_queries.sql.)
/E (passengers, 28 flights, 50 bookings and so on\). The queries demonstrate filtering with WHERE, sorting with ORDER BY, grouping with GROUP BY, filtering groups with HAVING, and the aggregate functions COUNT\(\), SUM\(\), AVG\(\), MIN\(\) and MAX\(\). Each query is followed by its output and a short explanation. Section 7 adds INSERT, UPDATE and DELETE statements. All commands are also in the script basic_queries.sql.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
