2074 0 obj
<<
/Title (The queries show how SQL retrieves exactly the data the airline needs. WHERE selects rows, ORDER BY arranges them, aggregate functions summarize them, GROUP BY summarizes per category \(status, payment method, seat class, aircraft\), and HAVING keeps only the groups that meet a condition, such as flights with at least four bookings or routes with a high average fare. Combined with joins, these clauses turn the nine related tables into answers about revenue, load, customer behaviour and fleet use.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2042 0 R
>>
endobj
